 "text": "Hello, how's your day? Well, the first step is to find a damp, woody kindling. You can use pine cones, dry twigs, or any other kindling that's damp. Then, take a piece of wood that's been in the rain, and rub it well against the damp kindling. Keep rubbing until the wood feels dry, and the kindling is all smoky. Sure, I do. I'd love to see yours. Well, it depends on the size of the pouch. Yes, you can. But you need to get the heat evenly. So, make sure you light the fire at the sides of the pouch. Make sure it's completely out before you go to bed. You can use a small stick to smother the flames, and then let it cool down.",
